# The ledger of `bson`: what a program does with BSON documents and
# MongoDB's Extended JSON, measured against Go's
# `go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver/v2/bson` v2.10.0 (`go doc -all`, the module
# fetched into the scratch folder on 2026-11-18), Rust's `bson` crate 2.15.0
# (its rustdoc, built in the scratch folder the same day: the items of
# `all.html` and the methods of `Document`, `Bson`, `ObjectId`, `Decimal128`,
# `DateTime`, `Timestamp`, `Binary`, `Regex`, `RawDocument` and
# `RawDocumentBuf`) and Python's `bson` of pymongo 4.20.0 (`dir()` of the
# module, `json_util`, and its classes, installed into the scratch folder the
# same day).
#
# Every expected value of the tests was observed: pymongo 4.20.0 wrote the
# bytes and the canonical and relaxed Extended JSON of 69 documents of edge
# values (every type, every subtype, the doubles' and dates' edges, the
# Decimal128 clamps), decoded by hand-built bytes of the five deprecated
# types, and answered the Decimal128 texts and encodings, the UUID byte
# orders, the vectors' bytes and refusals, and the ObjectId times.

capability bson/value  a document's every value held exactly, the deprecated types included
  heroes  bson.Value, bson.Document, bson.Field, bson.ObjectId, bson.Decimal128, bson.Timestamp
  go      D, E, M, A, Binary, CodeWithScope, DBPointer, DateTime, Decimal128, JavaScript, MaxKey, MinKey, Null, ObjectID, Regex, Symbol, Timestamp, Undefined, RawValue, Type, Type.String, Type.IsValid
  rust    Bson, Document, JavaScriptCodeWithScope, DbPointer, Timestamp, Regex, Binary, spec::ElementType, spec::BinarySubtype
  python  SON, Int64, Code, Regex, Binary, Timestamp, MinKey, MaxKey, ObjectId, Decimal128, DatetimeMS, the BSON* type constants
  note    a document keeps its order and may hold a name twice, as Go's D and Rust's Document do; pymongo's dict holds a name once

capability bson/encode  a document written as its bytes
  heroes  bson.encode
  go      Marshal, Encoder.Encode, NewEncoder
  rust    to_vec, Document::to_writer, RawDocumentBuf::from_document
  python  encode, BSON.encode
  note    a regex's options are written sorted and an array's names as 0, 1, ..., as pymongo writes them; a name or pattern holding a zero byte is refused, `invalid`; a double is written by `math.f64_to_bits`, exact for every float but a NaN, whose sign and payload no route of Rebel keeps: every NaN is read and written as the quiet NaN, 0x7ff8000000000000, where Go and Rust keep a NaN's bits

capability bson/decode  bytes read into a document, every length and every text checked, the nesting bounded
  heroes  bson.decode, bson.decode_with, bson.DecodeOptions, bson.strict_decode_options, bson.DEFAULT_MAX_DEPTH
  go      Unmarshal, Decoder.Decode, NewDecoder, ReadDocument
  rust    from_slice, from_reader, Document::from_reader, RawDocument::from_bytes
  python  decode, BSON.decode
  note    a boolean other than 0 or 1, a subtype 2 whose inner length disagrees and a code with scope whose lengths disagree are refused, as pymongo refuses them; an array's names are not read

capability bson/decode-lossy  text that is not UTF-8 read with U+FFFD
  heroes  bson.DecodeOptions.lossy_text
  go      -
  rust    from_slice_utf8_lossy, from_reader_utf8_lossy, Document::from_reader_utf8_lossy
  python  CodecOptions(unicode_decode_error_handler="replace")
  note    Go's driver does not check UTF-8 at all; here a text must be UTF-8 unless this is asked

capability bson/stream  the documents of a stream or a dump read one after another
  heroes  bson.decode_next, bson.decode_all, bson.Decoded
  go      Decoder.Decode, NewDecoder
  rust    -
  python  decode_all, decode_iter, decode_file_iter
  note    a file is read whole by `fs` or `io` first; `decode_next` answers where the next document begins

capability bson/validate  bytes checked for one well-formed document
  heroes  bson.is_valid
  go      Raw.Validate, RawElement.Validate, RawValue.Validate, RawArray.Validate
  rust    RawDocument::from_bytes
  python  is_valid

capability bson/raw-lookup  one field read out of a document's bytes without decoding the rest
  heroes  bson.lookup
  go      Raw.Lookup, Raw.LookupErr, Raw.Index, Raw.IndexErr, Raw.Elements, Raw.Values, RawElement.Key, RawElement.Value, RawArray.Index, RawArray.Values
  rust    RawDocument::get, RawDocument::get_str, RawDocument::get_i32, RawDocument::get_i64, RawDocument::get_f64, RawDocument::get_bool, RawDocument::get_document, RawDocument::get_array, RawDocument::get_binary, RawDocument::get_object_id, RawDocument::get_datetime, RawDocument::get_timestamp, RawDocument::get_regex, RawDocument::iter, RawDocumentBuf, RawBson, RawBsonRef, RawArray
  python  RawBSONDocument, RawBSONDocument.raw
  note    only the fields before the one found are walked, by their lengths; the field found is read whole

capability bson/fields  a document's fields read, set, removed and listed
  heroes  bson.member, bson.has_member, bson.with_member, bson.without_member, bson.names_of
  go      D.Map (gone in v2), M, E
  rust    Document::get, Document::insert, Document::remove, Document::contains_key, Document::keys, Document::values, Document::iter, Document::len, Document::is_empty, Document::entry, Document::clear, Document::extend
  python  dict's own operations, SON
  note    `len` and iteration are the built-ins' on `doc.fields`; a name that stands twice: `member` reads the first, `with_member` sets the first, `without_member` removes all

capability bson/path  a value reached by a dotted path, as a query names one
  heroes  bson.value_at
  go      Raw.Lookup with several keys, RawValue.Document
  rust    -
  python  -

capability bson/typed-reading  a value read as a given type, failing on another
  heroes  bson.text_of, bson.int_of, bson.number_of, bson.bool_of, bson.document_of, bson.items_of, bson.object_id_of, bson.bytes_of, bson.instant_of, bson.decimal_of, bson.kind_of, bson.type_code_of
  go      RawValue.StringValue, RawValue.Int32, RawValue.Int64, RawValue.AsInt64, RawValue.AsFloat64, RawValue.Double, RawValue.Boolean, RawValue.Document, RawValue.Array, RawValue.ObjectID, RawValue.Binary, RawValue.DateTime, RawValue.Time, RawValue.Decimal128, RawValue.Regex, RawValue.Timestamp, RawValue.JavaScript, RawValue.CodeWithScope, RawValue.DBPointer, RawValue.Symbol, RawValue.IsNumber, the *OK forms of each
  rust    Bson::as_str, Bson::as_i32, Bson::as_i64, Bson::as_f64, Bson::as_bool, Bson::as_document, Bson::as_array, Bson::as_object_id, Bson::as_datetime, Bson::as_timestamp, Bson::as_null, Bson::as_symbol, Bson::as_db_pointer, Bson::element_type, Document::get_str, Document::get_i32, Document::get_i64, Document::get_f64, Document::get_bool, Document::get_document, Document::get_array, Document::get_object_id, Document::get_datetime, Document::get_timestamp, Document::get_binary_generic, Document::get_decimal128, Document::is_null
  python  -
  note    `int_of` reads a double that is a whole number too, since servers answer counts and `ok` as doubles; a `match` on `Value` reads the rest

capability bson/int  an integer written at the narrowest type that holds it
  heroes  bson.from_int
  go      Encoder.IntMinSize
  rust    -
  python  Int64, and int encoded as int32 where it fits

capability bson/object-id  ObjectIds made, read, written and dated
  heroes  bson.ObjectIdMaker, bson.object_id_maker, bson.next_object_id, bson.object_id_at, bson.object_id_from_parts, bson.parse_object_id, bson.format_object_id, bson.object_id_from_bytes, bson.time_of, bson.is_object_id
  go      NewObjectID, NewObjectIDFromTimestamp, ObjectIDFromHex, NilObjectID, ObjectID.Hex, ObjectID.String, ObjectID.Timestamp, ObjectID.IsZero, ObjectID.MarshalText, ObjectID.UnmarshalText, ObjectID.MarshalJSON, ObjectID.UnmarshalJSON
  rust    oid::ObjectId::new, ObjectId::from_bytes, ObjectId::from_parts, ObjectId::parse_str, ObjectId::to_hex, ObjectId::timestamp, ObjectId::bytes
  python  ObjectId(), ObjectId.from_datetime, ObjectId.is_valid, ObjectId.generation_time, ObjectId.binary, str(ObjectId)
  note    the maker is a value the program holds, its five bytes and its counter drawn from the system's generator for keys, since the language has no mutable global; a zero id is `object_id_from_bytes` of twelve zeros

capability bson/datetime  a UTC datetime to and from an instant
  heroes  bson.from_instant, bson.instant_of
  go      NewDateTimeFromTime, DateTime.Time, DateTime.MarshalJSON, DateTime.UnmarshalJSON
  rust    DateTime::from_millis, DateTime::now, DateTime::timestamp_millis, DateTime::from_system_time, DateTime::to_system_time, DateTime::parse_rfc3339_str, DateTime::try_to_rfc3339_string, DateTime::builder, DateTime::checked_duration_since, DateTime::saturating_duration_since, DateTime::saturating_add_millis, DateTime::saturating_add_duration
  python  datetime, DatetimeMS, DatetimeMS.as_datetime, DatetimeConversion
  note    an instant is cut to the millisecond toward the past; the text and the arithmetic are `time`'s (`time.format`, `time.add`); a datetime outside an instant's 292 years either side of 1970 is held as its milliseconds and `instant_of` fails `does_not_fit`

capability bson/timestamp  a replication timestamp held and ordered
  heroes  bson.Timestamp, bson.compare_timestamps
  go      Timestamp.After, Timestamp.Before, Timestamp.Compare, Timestamp.Equal, Timestamp.IsZero
  rust    Timestamp, Timestamp::time, Timestamp::increment
  python  Timestamp, Timestamp.time, Timestamp.inc, Timestamp.as_datetime

capability bson/binary  binary data of every subtype
  heroes  bson.Value.binary, bson.bytes_of, bson.SUBTYPE_GENERIC, bson.SUBTYPE_FUNCTION, bson.SUBTYPE_BINARY_OLD, bson.SUBTYPE_UUID_OLD, bson.SUBTYPE_UUID, bson.SUBTYPE_MD5, bson.SUBTYPE_ENCRYPTED, bson.SUBTYPE_COLUMN, bson.SUBTYPE_SENSITIVE, bson.SUBTYPE_VECTOR, bson.SUBTYPE_USER_DEFINED
  go      Binary, Binary.Equal, Binary.IsZero, the TypeBinary* constants
  rust    Binary, Binary::from_base64, spec::BinarySubtype
  python  Binary, Binary.subtype, the *_SUBTYPE constants
  note    subtype 2 is held without its inner length and written with it, as pymongo does

capability bson/uuid  a UUID in subtype 4 and in the three legacy orders of subtype 3
  heroes  bson.UuidRepresentation, bson.from_uuid, bson.uuid_of, bson.reordered
  go      -
  rust    Uuid, UuidRepresentation, Binary::from_uuid, Binary::from_uuid_with_representation, Binary::to_uuid
  python  Binary.from_uuid, Binary.as_uuid, UuidRepresentation, ALL_UUID_SUBTYPES
  note    a UUID is its sixteen bytes here, `uuid` sits in the same layer; the orders are those pymongo 4.20 wrote

capability bson/vector  a dense vector in subtype 9: int8, float32 and packed bits
  heroes  bson.Vector, bson.from_vector, bson.vector_of
  go      Vector, NewVector, NewVectorFromBinary, NewPackedBitVector, Vector.Binary, Vector.Int8, Vector.Float32, Vector.PackedBit, Vector.Type
  rust    binary::Vector, binary::PackedBitVector
  python  Binary.from_vector, Binary.as_vector, BinaryVector, BinaryVectorDtype
  note    padding bits that are not zero are refused on reading too, where pymongo 4.20 only warns

capability bson/regex  a regular expression held and its options ordered
  heroes  bson.Value.regex, bson.from_regex
  go      Regex, Regex.Equal, Regex.IsZero, Regex.String
  rust    Regex, Regex::new
  python  Regex, Regex.from_native, Regex.try_compile
  note    the pattern is the server's PCRE and is not compiled here; `regex` matches Rebel's own syntax, not PCRE, so try_compile has no counterpart

capability bson/decimal128  Decimal128 read, written, and crossed to `big`, exactly
  heroes  bson.parse_decimal128, bson.format_decimal128, bson.from_decimal, bson.decimal_of
  go      ParseDecimal128, ParseDecimal128FromBigInt, NewDecimal128, Decimal128.String, Decimal128.BigInt, Decimal128.IsNaN, Decimal128.IsInf, Decimal128.IsZero, Decimal128.GetBytes
  rust    Decimal128, Decimal128::from_bytes, Decimal128::bytes, Decimal128::from_str, Decimal128::to_string
  python  Decimal128, Decimal128.to_decimal, Decimal128.from_bid, Decimal128.bid
  note    a text that needs rounding fails `invalid`, as pymongo's context traps it; zeros are clamped and trailing zeros moved into the exponent as pymongo does; a negative zero keeps its sign in the bytes and the text and is zero in a `big.Decimal`

capability bson/dbref  the DBRef convention read and written
  heroes  bson.DBRef, bson.from_dbref, bson.dbref_of
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  DBRef, DBRef.as_doc, DBRef.collection, DBRef.id, DBRef.database

capability bson/code  JavaScript code, with and without a scope
  heroes  bson.Value.javascript, bson.Value.javascript_with_scope
  go      JavaScript, CodeWithScope, CodeWithScope.String
  rust    Bson::JavaScriptCode, Bson::JavaScriptCodeWithScope
  python  Code, Code.scope

capability bson/extjson-out  a document written as Extended JSON v2, canonical or relaxed
  heroes  bson.to_json, bson.format_json, bson.value_to_json, bson.JsonMode
  go      MarshalExtJSON, MarshalExtJSONIndent, IndentExtJSON, NewExtJSONValueWriter
  rust    Bson::into_canonical_extjson, Bson::into_relaxed_extjson, Document's Display
  python  json_util.dumps, json_util.default, CANONICAL_JSON_OPTIONS, RELAXED_JSON_OPTIONS, JSONOptions, JSONMode
  note    canonical text is pymongo 4.20's byte for byte on 69 documents; relaxed differs in two places: an int64 past 2^53 stays `$numberLong`, so it reads back exactly, and a double that is a whole number is written as an integer (`json.Value` holds no point), so it reads back as an int32; indented text is `json.format_indented`

capability bson/extjson-in  a document read from Extended JSON v2, canonical, relaxed and the legacy forms
  heroes  bson.from_json, bson.parse_json, bson.value_from_json
  go      UnmarshalExtJSON, NewExtJSONValueReader
  rust    Bson::try_from(serde_json::Value), Document::try_from
  python  json_util.loads, json_util.object_hook, LEGACY_JSON_OPTIONS read
  note    a malformed wrapper fails with the JSON pointer of its place; `{"$regex": "a"}` alone is a query operator's document, where pymongo reads a regex (both query the same); a date's text of any year is read

capability bson/extjson-legacy-out  Extended JSON written in its legacy v1 form or the shell's
  heroes  refused: v1 and the shell's `ObjectId("...")` are superseded by v2 and the shell's form is no JSON; both are read where they are JSON
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  LEGACY_JSON_OPTIONS (writing), DatetimeRepresentation.LEGACY, DatetimeRepresentation.NUMBERLONG, DatetimeRepresentation.ISO8601

capability bson/struct-mapping  a record of the program filled from a document by its field names
  heroes  refused: the language has no reflection; a program writes each field with `Record::field` names (spec § 9), which the compiler checks
  go      Marshal and Unmarshal of structs, struct tags, Marshaler, Unmarshaler, ValueMarshaler, ValueUnmarshaler, KeyMarshaler, KeyUnmarshaler, Zeroer, MarshalValue, UnmarshalValue, Encoder.OmitEmpty, Encoder.NilSliceAsEmpty, Encoder.NilMapAsEmpty, Encoder.NilByteSliceAsEmpty, Encoder.OmitZeroStruct, Encoder.ErrorOnInlineDuplicates, Encoder.StringifyMapKeysWithFmt, Encoder.UseJSONStructTags, Decoder.DefaultDocumentM, Decoder.DefaultDocumentMap, Decoder.UseJSONStructTags, Decoder.ZeroMaps, Decoder.ZeroStructs, Decoder.AllowTruncatingDoubles, Decoder.BinaryAsSlice, Decoder.ObjectIDAsHexString, Decoder.UseLocalTimeZone
  rust    to_bson, to_bson_with_options, to_document, to_document_with_options, from_bson, from_bson_with_options, from_document, from_document_with_options, ser::Serializer, de::Deserializer, serde_helpers
  python  CodecOptions.document_class, TypeCodec, TypeRegistry, TypeEncoder, TypeDecoder

capability bson/codec-registry  encoders and decoders registered per type at run time
  heroes  refused: a registry dispatches on a value's dynamic type, which the language has not; a `match` on `Value` is the dispatch
  go      Registry, NewRegistry, NewMgoRegistry, NewRespectNilValuesMgoRegistry, Registry.RegisterTypeEncoder, Registry.RegisterTypeDecoder, Registry.RegisterKindEncoder, Registry.RegisterKindDecoder, Registry.RegisterInterfaceEncoder, Registry.RegisterInterfaceDecoder, Registry.RegisterTypeMapEntry, Registry.LookupEncoder, Registry.LookupDecoder, Registry.LookupTypeMapEntry, ValueEncoder, ValueDecoder, ValueEncoderFunc, ValueDecoderFunc, EncodeContext, DecodeContext, Encoder.SetRegistry, Decoder.SetRegistry
  rust    -
  python  TypeRegistry, CodecOptions.type_registry

capability bson/streaming-writers  a document read and written token by token
  heroes  refused: a document is small (16 MiB on a server) and read whole; `lookup` reads one field without the rest
  go      ValueReader, ValueWriter, DocumentReader, DocumentWriter, ArrayReader, ArrayWriter, NewDocumentReader, NewDocumentWriter, ReadArray
  rust    RawDocument::iter_elements, RawElement
  python  -

dropped
  go      ErrDecodeToNil, ErrEOA, ErrEOD, ErrInvalidHex, ErrInvalidJSON, ErrNilContext, ErrNilReader, ErrNilRegistry, DecodeError, DecodeError.Keys, ValueEncoderError, ValueDecoderError, TransitionError: error types, here codes and messages; D.String, M.String, Raw.String, RawValue.DebugString, RawElement.DebugString, RawArray.DebugString: debugging text, here `format_json`; Encoder.Reset, Decoder.Reset: reuse of a buffer
  rust    the Error types of each module and their Result aliases; Document::get_*_mut and the *_mut accessors: a value is changed with `with_member`; the serde traits' impls (serialize, deserialize), the tap and pipe helpers of the documentation's blanket impls
  python  InvalidBSON, InvalidDocument, InvalidStringData, InvalidId: here codes; has_c: whether a C extension is loaded; gen_list_name and the module's imported names (Any, Callable, Mapping, ...); CodecOptions.tz_aware and tzinfo: a datetime here is UTC by definition
